Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-30
Subject: Guard arm aasmcpu next-instruction narrowing cast
License: expat

`compiler/arm/aasmcpu.pas` checks whether `curtai.next` starts a case-jump
table with:

  taicpu(curtai.next).typ=ait_instruction

That narrows the base `tai` node to `taicpu` before proving it is actually
an instruction node.  Under native FPC this old-style cast slips by, but the
translated C++ stage1 compiler turns it into a concrete downcast.  During the
armhf bootstrap, `curtai.next` can be a `tai_function_name`, and UBSan then
correctly reports the bad cast before `data2inc` finishes compiling.

Fix this the same way as the other bootstrap-source type guards: check the
base `tai.typ` first, then narrow to `taicpu` only after short-circuiting has
proved the node is an instruction.

--- a/compiler/arm/aasmcpu.pas
+++ b/compiler/arm/aasmcpu.pas
@@ -715,7 +715,7 @@
 
             { special case for case jump tables }
             if assigned(curtai.next) and
-              (taicpu(curtai.next).typ=ait_instruction) and
+              (tai(curtai.next).typ=ait_instruction) and
               (taicpu(curtai.next).opcode=A_LDR) and
               (taicpu(curtai.next).oper[0]^.typ=top_reg) and
               (taicpu(curtai.next).oper[0]^.reg=NR_PC) then
